      "description": "History after 10000 small edits (70 percent entity moves, 20 percent counter, 10 percent nested view changes), compared with keeping a full snapshot of the tracked state after every edit. Serialized size is counted in characters of JSON (the content is ASCII, so characters are bytes). Heap is the retained size after forced collections, with the same store and edits without the feature subtracted. A snapshot is the set of references to the tracked slices after the edit, which is what a snapshot stack keeps. The checkpoint rows, the pending limit rows and the serialization rows use 1000 entities.",
